  {
   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "Show that f : R → R, f(x) = 3x + 2 is a bijection."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "One-one: 3x₁ + 2 = 3x₂ + 2 ⇒ x₁ = x₂."
    },
    {
     "en": "Onto: for any real y, take x = (y − 2)/3; then f(x) = y."
    },
    {
     "en": "Both hold, so f is a bijection."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "f is one-one and onto"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us solve this together. Show that f : R → R, f(x) = 3x + 2 is a bijection."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ex2",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "Is f : N → N, f(x) = x² one-one? Is it onto?"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "In N, x₁² = x₂² gives x₁ = x₂ (no negatives), so f is one-one."
    },
    {
     "en": "2 ∈ N, but no natural number has square 2."
    },
    {
     "en": "So f is not onto."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "One-one but not onto"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us solve this together. Is f : N → N, f(x) = x² one-one? Is it onto?"
   }
